On Nov 9, 2007 10:31 PM, Chris Capel <pdf23ds@gmail.com> wrote:
> I'm trying to get my parser to recognize selbri places so I can gloss
> them like jboski does. I don't think the grammar currently figures out
> which places the various terms fit. (I'm not sure it could
> gracefully.)

In principle it's probably impossible, because a selbri can have an
indefinite number of places. But even if we restrictit to idntifying the
first few, it would be extremely messy.

> So should I do this myself? If so, will handling SE, FA,
> CO, and modals be enough?

SE, CO, JAI and probably BE-BEI are needed to figure out the
place structure of the full selbri from the place sructure of the
component brivla.

FA, gihek, gek, VAU and all the termset stuff has to be taken into
account to figure out which slot a given term fills.

